All eight models come in from grade 5 (the mu-g5 rows' model_out and the mu-g6 rows' model_in); none is new in this
course. Each is retrieved in the first unit of year 6 that uses it.

| Model | Where it comes from | Introduced or first used here | Used again here |
|---|---|---|---|
| rhythm-syllables | Grade 5 (mu-g5-read, model_out) | Unit 1: rhythm syllables as the bridge to naming each rhythm symbol on the staff | Unit 5 (ties, syncopation, form and tempo signs, mu-g7-read), unit 9 (reading at sight, mu-g8-read); units 3, 7 and 11 use it to notate rhythm, as review |
| describe-interpret-judge | Grade 5 (mu-g5-respond, model_out) | Unit 1: describe the elements, name the setting, judge with the teacher's criteria | Unit 5 (sort, compare, criteria chosen, mu-g7-respond), unit 9 (whole programs, the student's criteria, mu-g8-respond); every unit's listening as review |
| expression-map | Grade 5 (mu-g5-express, model_out) | Unit 2: the student's own map of dynamics, tempo, articulation and tone color for a chosen piece | Unit 6 (two contrasting maps, mu-g7-express), unit 10 (the map explained and backed, mu-g8-express); every concert unit's rehearsal as review |
| listening-log | Grade 5 (mu-g5-choose, model_out) | Unit 2: picks for a purpose logged against the teacher's criteria | Unit 6 (a shared program, mu-g7-choose), unit 10 (a themed program with the student's criteria, mu-g8-choose); units 1, 5 and 9 log their listening works, as review |
| idea-bank | Grade 5 (mu-g5-invent, model_out) | Unit 3: phrase ideas banked for an AB or ABA piece | Unit 7 (variations of one theme, mu-g7-invent), unit 11 (sections and an introduction and coda, mu-g8-invent) |
| notation-ladder | Grade 5 (mu-g5-document, model_out) | Unit 3: the step from rhythm syllables to the full staff with chord symbols | Unit 7 (a chord sequence, mu-g7-document), unit 11 (a longer score, mu-g8-document) |
| critique-protocol | Grade 5 (mu-g5-revise, model_out) | Unit 1's one critique (describe, ask, suggest) retrieves it; unit 4 makes it the revision tool with the teacher's criteria | Unit 8 (criteria the student chooses, mu-g7-revise), unit 12 (choices justified, mu-g8-revise); every unit's critique as review |
| practice-plan | Grade 5 (mu-g5-perform, model_out) | Unit 4: the rehearsal plan with a readiness check against the teacher's criteria | Unit 8 (class-written criteria, mu-g7-perform), unit 12 (the student's own criteria, mu-g8-perform); units 2, 6 and 10 rehearse their performances with it, as review |

All eight go on to Level 1 (the mu-g9 rows' model_in).

