## Cross-subject

Two music rows of grades 6 to 8 carry a cross_subject lean (data/progressions/arts.csv): mu-g6-respond on ELA's
SL.6.1 and mu-g8-respond on ELA's W.8.1. Both are core courses (lesson 32); each lean is practiced, not owned, and
each has its "if later" line. STANDARD.md 6's music and math lean (note values as fractions) ended in grade 5
(mu-g5-read, math:5.NF.A.1); here dotted notes and ties are read as music signs only.

### English language arts, grade 6 (same year)

| Used here | Lean | ELA unit that teaches it | If ELA has not taught it yet |
|---|---|---|---|
| Unit 1 (year 6, days 1 to 18, weeks 1 to 9): talk about the listening works and the critique (mu-g6-respond) | SL.6.1 (discussion with evidence: coming prepared, rules and roles, questions, paraphrase) | ELA grade 6 unit 1 (days 1 to 32), which teaches the discussion routine (SL.6.1a to d) in weeks 1 to 7 | The music unit's discussion card gives the routine itself (come with the listening log marked, one speaker, a question back, say what you heard the last speaker say) and the teacher models it on the first listening day; nothing in the talk is scored as ELA |

### English language arts, grade 8 (same year)

| Used here | Lean | ELA unit that teaches it | If ELA has not taught it yet |
|---|---|---|---|
| Unit 9 (year 8, days 129 to 146, weeks 1 to 9): the written judgment with the student's own criteria (mu-g8-respond); unit 10's backed reading uses it again | W.8.1 (an argument supported by evidence) | ELA grade 8 unit 2 (days 31 to 62), which teaches argument writing in full (W.8.1a to e) in weeks 7 to 13 | Unit 9 teaches the short form it needs (a claim, evidence heard in the music, a reason) with a frame and a model; the item is scored on the music evidence only, never on argument conventions |

### Physical education, health and dance (boundaries)

Students move only to show a music idea (conducting a meter, body percussion, clapping a pattern); they do not dance
(the samba de roda circle and the powwow are studied by watching), since dance is its own course and its motor skill
is physical education's (STANDARD.md 6). Changing voices are named as a normal change in the safety bullet only; why
voices change is health's to teach, and no music unit teaches it. No lean either way.

### Social studies, grades 6 to 8

The settings of works (Tuva, Senegal, Ethiopia, Lebanon, Brazil, China, Korea) are taught by each unit on its own work cards (bar
criterion 7), using social studies' sourcing habit of who, when, where and for what; the unit teaches the setting
it uses itself. No lean either way.

