raft by draft. Mid-unit assessment: the second draft and its log entry, near day 64. Each item is marked met, partly or not yet. Out: rondo and ternary (Level 2). Tools: listening maps and the draft log, Curio Class's own | After unit 2 because the drafts grow from its sketch; the form analysis comes first in the unit because the drafts copy a studied form as a step, never as the end. Before unit 4 because revision to a final version needs drafts | Candidate: a binary or cyclical form from Africa or the Americas beside the three, by a living composer | Gamelan: studied by listening only, from the ensemble's or archive's own page and the community's published teaching; no student imitates court or ceremonial use, and the class composes its own cycle, never a copy (STANDARD.md 5 leave-out line). The sensitivity agent reads the archive's page first. Handy's blues are taught with their setting (the Mississippi Delta, Memphis); lyrics are not sung. Agent reads: sensitivity; safety (voice and sound). |
