r another class or families, with the family's yes (or the student's own at 18) for any showing outside class. End-of-unit evidence, id by id: MU:Pr5.1.C.Ia, a look-for on the kept rehearsal plan: repetition and variation marked; MU:Pr5.1.C.Ib, a written note after the dress rehearsal: how one performance carries elements, style and mood, against the set criteria; MU:Pr5.1.C.Ic, a look-for on the rehearsal log: one technique and one expression fix tried across the works; MU:Pr6.1.C.Ia, a look-for on the showing (live or the take): the performance with its spoken or written program note on how elements carry the aim; MU:Pr6.1.C.Ib, a written note after the concert: how the piece suited its audience and one change next; MU:Re9.1.C.Ia, a sitting item on an unseen public domain performance: how well its technique and expression work, in basic theory terms; MU:Re9.1.C.Ib, a look-for on the critique trail: one feedback given, one received and what it changed; MU:Cn11.0.C.Ia, a written note: one link from a studied work to another art, subject, setting or daily life. Two mid-unit assessments: the rehearsal plan (near day 128) and the critique trail (near day 142). Each item is marked met, partly or not yet. Out: historical setting in the plan (Level 2). Tools: the rehearsal plan form, the critique card and the program note sheet, Curio Class's own; a recording device of the school's, optional | Last in the level because the concert performs the level's final versions and ends the year; the practice-plan and describe-interpret-judge models come back from grade 8 here, where they are first needed. Its showing (weeks 30 and 31) is its own assessment, before the year-end check | Candidate: a Native American or Asian performance for the critique sitting, for range | Recording: no student is recorded without the family's yes (or their own at 18); a face or voice is never required (hands, the score or the sound alone will do); a student who does not want to be recorded is observed live and the teacher's mark stands; takes stay on the student's, family's or school's own device. No student performs alone unless they choose to: every piece has a group or doubled version. Hazards and controls: voice rest after long rehearsals; headphones at a low set volume. Agent reads: sensitivity; safety (voice and sound). |

